 and Hasse were now nearly one lap behind the leaders.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":4},{"lap":40,"text":"After 40 laps, mid-race, Caracciola stopped for fuel and rear tires in 26.6 seconds.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":40,"text":"Rosemeyer equals Brauchitsch's record lap of 2m11.4s and is second again, 24 seconds behind.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":40,"text":"After 40 laps, mid-race, Caracciola stopped for fuel and rear tires in 26.6 seconds.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":40,"text":"Rosemeyer equals Brauchitsch's record lap of 2m11.4s and is second again, 24 seconds behind.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":42,"text":"Dobson stops to change the magneto, a 14-minute job with the one taken from Martin's retired ERA.","q":false,"c":7},{"lap":42,"text":"Dobson stops to change the magneto, a 14-minute job with the one taken from Martin's retired ERA.","q":false,"c":7},{"lap":50,"text":"On the 50th lap Brauchitsch led at 83.17 mph by 26 seconds to Rosemeyer and 82 seconds to Caracciola in third place with a long gap to M\u00fcller and Hasse even further behind.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":50,"text":"On the 50th lap Brauchitsch led at 83.17 mph by 26 seconds to Rosemeyer and 82 seconds to Caracciola in third place with a long gap to M\u00fcller and Hasse even further behind.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":51,"text":"At 51 laps, after changing a plug, Mays had to retire the ERA with useless brakes.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":10},{"lap":51,"text":"At 51 laps, after changing a plug, Mays had to retire the ERA with useless brakes.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":10},{"lap":52,"text":"Brauchitsch stops for rear tyres; Rosemeyer passes and leads by 11 seconds.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":52,"text":"Brauchitsch stops for rear tyres; Rosemeyer passes and leads by 11 seconds.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":60,"text":"By the 60th lap Rosemeyer averaged 83.06 mph and increased his advantage to 20 seconds over Brauchitsch with 